ith their partner samantha  wishes that she could have a body and  would be able to walk next to him  theo finally meets his date the date  goes well they share the same hobbies  and similarities both are laughing at  each other's jokes but the happy moment  doesn't last long  theo hesitates to promise that he will  see her again disappointing the woman as  she doesn't want her time to be wasted  for somebody who doesn't want to commit  to a relationship so she insults him and  goes away  at night he shares his date experience  to samantha saying that it was kind of a  weird date after that samantha and  theo's intimacy grows through a verbal  sexual encounter both of them start  fantasizing if samantha was sleeping  next to him right now and cuddling  together they develop a relationship  that reflects positively in theaters  writing at the office and well-being as  well as samantha's enthusiasm to grow  and learn on their sunday adventure theo  seems to have transformed himself into a  better version of himself happy and  energetic  samantha asks how it feels to be married  theo says that marriage is hard but  there is something that feels good about  sharing your life with somebody  he adds that catherine came from a  background where nothing was ever good  enough but because of their relationship  both of them were allowing each other to  fail and enjoy things making them grow  and change together  after work theater approaches amy and  she reveals that she is going to end her  8 years relationship with charles  because she finds charles is too  overwhelming  amy didn't want to be told where she had  to put her shoes but charles insisted  amy to place her shoes at certain places  causing them to have arguments for 10  minutes before amy decided to divorce  her husband later on theo explains to  samantha that he and amy were lovers  once in college but only in a short  period of time before he felt like it  was better to be friends  after both of them are now uno